# Accessibility

- Target WCAG 2.2 AA and use semantic HTML before ARIA.
- Every interaction must work by keyboard with visible focus and logical order.
- Give controls accessible names, forms persistent labels, and errors that are
  announced and associated with their fields.
- Use accessible Radix/shadcn primitives for dialogs, menus, and popovers without
  removing required semantics.
- Maintain sufficient contrast and never rely on color alone.
- Honor `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- Provide accessible table or textual equivalents for charts.
- Verify usability at 375px and larger breakpoints; replace dense mobile tables
  with meaningful summaries where needed.
